message: "If you use this software or benchmark in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Selective Escalation of Uncertain Streaming Sensor Anomalies via Tiered Decision Architectures"
abstract: "Bounded Decision Tiering (BDT) is a stream processing architecture for real-time sensor telemetry anomaly detection using Apache Flink, Apache Kafka, in-JVM ONNX ensembles, and epistemic uncertainty gating. By selectively escalating ambiguous stream events (~20.5%) to an asynchronous XGBoost decision sidecar, detection F1-score is boosted from 0.4125 to 0.8238 (+99.7% gain) and false positive rates are slashed by 86.2% (from 7.20% down to 1.00%), while preserving sustained streaming throughput of 9,885 events/sec with only 0.7% system overhead."
version: 1.0.0
